# Golden image / 2026-27

Current lifecycle is config-driven through `scripts/config/config.toml` and `scripts/mct-vm.py`.

Before a new classroom image round:

1. Review `scripts/config/config.toml`, especially `[workflow]`, `[golden_image]` and `[run]`.
2. Review/update `scripts/config/rollout.csv` and run `./scripts/mct-vm.py generate-nix` if the
   active VM/student mapping changed.
3. Build the generic QCOW2 (`nix build .#qcow2`) and place/name it as configured.
4. Run `./scripts/mct-vm.py prepare-golden`.
5. Work through `doc/golden-phase2-checklist.md`. `prepare-golden` has already
   installed the reviewed Continue config so the real Continue connection can be
   tested during this one manual VM session.
6. Shut the golden VM down cleanly as the final checklist step.
7. Run `./scripts/mct-vm.py finalize-golden`; this removes Bash/Chrome
   manual-work traces without deleting Chrome preferences, installs the managed
   start page, and cleanly freezes the golden image. It deliberately does not
   verify or replace the Continue config.
8. Run `clone`, then `individualize` (pilot with `[run].only_vms` first).
9. Run `prepare-images`, `update-csv`, then `rollout`.

Lockdown and classroom are alternative workflow modes. Lockdown has different
seat assignments and is intentionally not being expanded/reworked right now.
